# pod_ulx3s.lpf — Lattice Preference File (constraints) for WaveTensor Pod
#                 on ULX3S (CS-ULX3S-03, LFE5U-85F-6BG381C).
#
# This is the Stage 1 constraint file. It is the LPF-format equivalent of
# synth/constraints/pod.xdc (Vivado) — currently a minimal OOC-like set
# (just clock definition + reset false path). Real ULX3S pin assignments
# will be added when the board arrives and we lift the Pod up into a full
# design with visible pins.
#
# TODO(Stage 1 Board arrival):
#   * add pin assignments (LOCATE COMP ...) for:
#     - clk    → ULX3S 25 MHz oscillator on pin G2 (needs PLL to 100 MHz)
#     - rst    → ULX3S user button (BTN0 on pin R1)
#     - LED status → 8 LEDs on pins B2, C2, C1, D2, D1, E2, E1, H3
#     - USB CDC UART TX/RX → FTDI FT231X on pins M1, L4 (per ULX3S schematic)
#   * add PLL configuration (25 MHz → 100 MHz core clock)
#   * add DDR3 constraints if we bring up the on-board SDRAM for host transport
#   * verify the CS-ULX3S-03 revision — ULX3S SKUs have multiple hardware revs
#     (v1.7, v2.0, v3.0.7, v3.1.7). Pinout differences exist.

# --- Clock definition ---------------------------------------------------
FREQUENCY PORT "clk" 100 MHZ;

# --- Reset is asynchronous ---------------------------------------------
# Nextpnr does not need an explicit false path directive for async reset;
# the RTL uses `posedge rst` in flops which nextpnr recognizes as an async
# preset/clear input and does not include on the timing graph.

# --- Pin assignments (deferred, see TODO above) ------------------------
# LOCATE COMP "clk"     SITE "G2";
# LOCATE COMP "rst"     SITE "R1";
# LOCATE COMP "led[0]"  SITE "B2";
# IOBUF PORT "clk" IO_TYPE=LVCMOS33;

# --- OOC / synthesis-only note -----------------------------------------
# Currently Pod's full I/O surface (416-bit instruction bus + 80-bit tag +
# 64-bit dual payload) far exceeds ULX3S's ~100 user I/O pins. For Stage 1
# we will not expose the raw Pod ports directly — a thin wrapper (e.g.,
# `Pod_ulx3s_top.v`) will:
#   1. Instantiate Pod with the default geometry (2,2)x(2,2) = 16 PE.
#   2. Feed instructions from an on-chip ROM or FIFO fed by USB CDC UART.
#   3. Route results back over the same UART.
#   4. Expose only clk/rst/UART/LED to real pins.
#
# The wrapper design is deferred to Stage 1 board bring-up.
